From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenCCU <noreply@openccu>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 11:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] webui: sort devdescr inputs before JS generation

Upstream: Not applicable
Signed-off-by: GitHub Copilot <noreply@github.com>

The DEVDB glob order is filesystem-dependent. This can change the generated
`webui.js` layout between builds and makes downstream rootfs patches brittle.

Sort the file list explicitly so generated output is deterministic.
---
 src/webui/www_source/create_devdescr_js.tcl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/webui/www_source/create_devdescr_js.tcl b/src/webui/www_source/create_devdescr_js.tcl
index 2f4b3df..f95dc5d 100755
--- a/src/webui/www_source/create_devdescr_js.tcl
+++ b/src/webui/www_source/create_devdescr_js.tcl
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@ proc DEV_getImagePath {key size} {
   return $path
 }
 
-set filelist [glob -nocomplain [file join "$DEVDB_DIRECTORY/*.tcl"]]
+set filelist [lsort [glob -nocomplain [file join "$DEVDB_DIRECTORY/*.tcl"]]]
   
 foreach file $filelist {
 
